<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Fitna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/656">656</a>–<a href="/years/661">661 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Fitna was the first civil war within the Muslim community, fought in 656–661 CE after the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a> Uthman. It pitted Caliph Ali against opponents including Mu'awiya, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, and ended with Ali's assassination and Mu'awiya's founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>. It closed the era of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> and laid the roots of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a>–Shi'a division.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-fitna.jpg" alt="First Fitna" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Al Ameer son · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_Fitna_Map,_Ali-Muawiya_Phase.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
